    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Helena West Side is bordered to the east by the city of Helena and to the northeast by the Helena Valley West Central CDP.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena_West_Side%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Route 12 runs through the community, leading east 3 miles to downtown Helena and west over the Continental Divide 40 miles to Interstate 90 at Garrison.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena_West_Side%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Helena grew along Last Chance Gulch and in 1875 became the Montana territorial capital.",
